---
title: "US 2.0.8, 2.0.10: View a Site's Details From the Map / Add links to Site Page"
config:
  theme: base
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 70
    boxMargin: 12
    diagramMarginX: 45
    diagramMarginY: 30
    messageMargin: 38
    noteMargin: 16
    mirrorActors: true
    width: 200
    height: 90
  themeVariables:
    background: "#ffffff"
    primaryColor: "#69a8ef"
    primaryBorderColor: "#333333"
    primaryTextColor: "#111111"
    actorBkg: "#69a8ef"
    actorBorder: "#333333"
    actorTextColor: "#111111"
    actorLineColor: "#555555"
    signalColor: "#333333"
    signalTextColor: "#111111"
    activationBkgColor: "#cdd3db"
    activationBorderColor: "#cdd3db"
    noteBkgColor: "#ffe344"
    noteBorderColor: "#d4ba24"
    noteTextColor: "#111111"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#ffffff"
    labelBoxBorderColor: "#555555"
    labelTextColor: "#111111"
    loopTextColor: "#111111"
    altBackground: "#ffffff"
  themeCSS: |
    .actor-line {
      stroke-dasharray: 10 10 !important;
      stroke-width: 1.25px !important;
    }
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Map as Steward map page<br/>(Proposed)
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant DB as Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL
    participant Site as Site page<br/>/detail/[namesite]

    Note over Steward,Site: Covers US 2.0.8, and US 2.0.10 on the Site page. The map page is Proposed (see US 2.0.1).<br/>getSiteByName and getFormResponsesBySite exist. The Site page uses the same functions.

    Steward->>Map: Select a Site on the map
    activate Map
    Map-->>Steward: Highlight only the new selection (2.0.1 AT4)
    Map->>Actions: getSiteByName(namesite) (exists)
    activate Actions
    Actions->>Actions: Check session and approved account (Proposed)
    Note right of Actions: Missing today: no access check.<br/>createServerSupabase bypasses RLS.
    Actions->>DB: Read W26_sites-pa where is_active,<br/>with W26_ab_counties and W26_form_responses dates
    activate DB
    DB-->>Actions: Site row or no row
    deactivate DB

    alt Site not found or inactive
        Actions-->>Map: Empty list
        Map-->>Steward: Show "Site not available"
    else Site found
        Actions-->>Map: Name, county, last inspection date
        Map-->>Steward: Open the detail view (AT1)
        Note right of Map: Same values as the Site page, because<br/>both use getSiteByName (AT2).
    end
    deactivate Actions

    opt Select "View SIRs" (AT3)
        Steward->>Map: Select "View SIRs"
        Map->>Site: Open /detail/[namesite]
        activate Site
        Site->>Actions: getFormResponsesBySite(namesite) (exists)
        activate Actions
        Actions->>Actions: Same session check as above (Proposed)
        Actions->>DB: Read active W26_form_responses and W26_answers
        activate DB
        DB-->>Actions: Past SIRs
        deactivate DB
        Actions-->>Site: Past SIRs
        deactivate Actions
        Site-->>Steward: Show past SIRs of the Site
        deactivate Site
    end
    deactivate Map

    opt Open an external link (US 2.0.10, UI only)
        Steward->>Site: Select the SAPAA website link or the iNaturalist link (Proposed)
        Site-->>Steward: Open the link in a new browser tab (target="_blank")
        Note right of Site: No server call. The link text is a short URL.<br/>Link source per Site is an open question.<br/>A possible source: legacy<br/>sites_report_fnr_test has sapaaweb<br/>and inatmap (FNR/src/services/<br/>database.ts:503).
    end
